WEBVTT

00:00:06.769 --> 00:00:09.769
Sorry about the heels. I need the inches.

00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:18.750
I'm not sure this is such a good idea.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:23.750
Look, either RAO Incorporated is throwing a Valentine's Day party for their workers behind this wall,

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.750
or they're running double shifts on a Saturday night, a total union violation.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.750
Lois, I'm sure someone is keeping an eye on this situation.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:41.710
Bingo.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:47.759
They are moving more tech equipment into that building than NASA.

00:00:47.759 --> 00:00:51.759
And if they're skulking around in the middle of the night, they are definitely hiding something.

00:00:51.759 --> 00:01:00.469
Good.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:01.469
Nice teddy.

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:03.469
next time by her silk one. She's not six years old.

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:06.469
You know, Lois, I think we should drop this store.

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:08.469
You sound like you want it all to yourself.

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:11.469
Wait, is there something about that tower that you're not telling me?

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:15.709
No.

00:01:15.709 --> 00:01:18.709
It's Valentine's Day. We should be out having dinner together.

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:20.709
By candlelight.

00:01:20.709 --> 00:01:25.709
Clark. Valentine's Day is just a smarmy hallmark holiday engineered by corporate executives

00:01:25.709 --> 00:01:30.709
to convince people to spend hard-earned money on dead flowers and overpriced meals.

00:01:30.709 --> 00:01:34.469
But not you too.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:36.819
Lois.

00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:39.819
You're kind of overreacting, even for you.

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:45.819
History has proven that if I embrace B-Day in any romantic way at all,

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:48.819
it always ends in disaster.

00:01:48.819 --> 00:01:50.819
Valentine for the lady?

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:54.159
No, thank you. She doesn't really...

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:55.159
Actually.

00:01:55.159 --> 00:02:00.750
What? I didn't have dinner.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.750
Happy Valentine's Day.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:20.599
Easy with a pixie dust, their Tinkerbell.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:29.900
Looks like it's too late to file that story anyway.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.900
It's never too early for nachos, and it's never too late.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.400
And it's never too late for hard-hitting journalism.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.900
Lois, maybe we should put our relationship before our work,

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.900
just for tonight.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:38.900
Old hands?

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.400
You could come a courting on your horse and buggy?

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.900
All we need is a chaperone.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.900
Sounds mighty traditional.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.900
And what's wrong with that?

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.900
With all of our cross-text messages lately,

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.900
I thought maybe sometimes.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:58.580
I want us to have a more traditional relationship.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:07.939
Lane.

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:10.939
The REO is scheduled a ribbon cutting.

00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:13.939
We've been cutting for the solar tower in two days.

00:03:13.939 --> 00:03:15.939
I'm gonna need the expose now.

00:03:15.939 --> 00:03:17.939
Two days.

00:03:17.939 --> 00:03:19.939
Lois, maybe I should check on those building permits

00:03:19.939 --> 00:03:20.939
that you were talking about.

00:03:20.939 --> 00:03:24.939
And you wanted to avoid the whole Valentine's Day thing, thing, right?

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:28.939
Anything for your career, sweetie?

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:41.520
Here's the scoop, buddy.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.020
A traditional woman does not spend her time in the office

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:49.680
when she can be at home taking care of her man.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.680
I quit.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:04:56.269
I was gonna ask you for the lowdown on your V day with Lois.

00:04:56.269 --> 00:04:58.269
but something about you being here with me

00:04:58.269 --> 00:05:00.269
tells me it didn't go over so well.

00:05:00.269 --> 00:05:02.269
Give the passports and ID cards ready?

00:05:02.269 --> 00:05:06.449
Or we could get right down to business.

00:05:06.449 --> 00:05:10.449
All the materials you would ever need to escape your life

00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:11.449
and start a new one.

00:05:11.449 --> 00:05:13.449
Thanks, Chloe. You're a lifesaver.

00:05:13.449 --> 00:05:16.449
If by that you mean sweet on the outside and empty in the middle,

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.449
that's pretty much exactly how I feel right now.

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:21.449
Look, I realize you're not on board with me helping the Candorians.

00:05:21.449 --> 00:05:24.449
Yeah, well, you know how it is.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:27.449
You find out that one of them skewers you to death

00:05:27.449 --> 00:05:28.449
in the post-apocalyptic future.

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:30.449
you kind of lose interest.

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:33.449
I know it seems like I may have overlooked some of their mistakes.

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:34.449
Mistakes?

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:38.449
By mistakes do you mean them building a tower so they can give themselves power to take over the world?

00:05:38.449 --> 00:05:40.449
I'm going to lead them to a better place.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:43.449
The tower will be completed in two days.

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:47.449
Granted, they haven't got the satellites up and running to change the atmosphere,

00:05:47.449 --> 00:05:49.449
but come on, Clark.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.449
We both know one of them killed your father.

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:57.449
Maybe it would just be safer if we sent the Kandorians to the Phantom Zone.

00:05:57.449 --> 00:06:02.339
I know that you're saying that because you want to protect people.

00:06:02.339 --> 00:06:05.339
But right now, I want you to focus on watching my back.

00:06:05.339 --> 00:06:11.079
Leave the rest of the planet to me.

00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:19.040
Clark, I will protect you.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.040
No matter what it takes.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:32.029
Who those men are?

00:06:32.029 --> 00:06:35.029
Alia? I have your papers.

00:06:35.029 --> 00:06:38.339
It's your new life.

00:06:38.339 --> 00:06:40.339
You have your own identities.

00:06:40.339 --> 00:06:53.000
I misjudged you, Kello.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:03.290
I was born into the military.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.290
I never had a choice to live as a civilian.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:10.110
I can't repay you.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:14.420
Tell me who killed my father.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:20.930
I know that Zod took him from Tess.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.930
Was he the last one to see Jerelle alive?

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:26.930
I know you want justice, but be careful.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:32.930
Zod has a lot of loyal followers, and if you go after him, it'll be warm.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:08:07.420
Hey, sweetie pie. Welcome home.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.420
Loz, what's going on?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.819
I moved in.

00:08:11.819 --> 00:08:20.189
But don't worry, I'm camped out into the guest room until we get engaged.

00:08:20.189 --> 00:08:21.189
Engaged?

00:08:21.189 --> 00:08:34.299
Move over Betty Crocker.

00:08:34.299 --> 00:08:37.299
I have got this cooking thing down.

00:08:37.299 --> 00:08:38.299
How's your pot roast?

00:08:38.299 --> 00:08:42.980
Oh, it's delicious.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:47.090
Wonderful.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:50.090
It was really sweet of you to do all of this.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:54.090
Well, I am just so proud of you for bringing home the bacon.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.090
The least I can do is cook it up in a pan.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:04.779
I never let you forget that you're the man.

00:09:04.779 --> 00:09:09.980
Well, did something happen?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.980
You just seem so cheerful, but...

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.980
Well, you said you wanted a more traditional,

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:20.980
relationship and you were very persuasive.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:23.980
What if I missed the old Lois?

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:27.360
Too late.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.360
I quit my job at the planet.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.360
You did what?

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.360
Yeah.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.360
Now, instead of being chained to a desk all day,

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.360
I get to be your ball inching.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:47.340
Moss, you can't quit reporting. That job is your life.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.340
Well, now my life is with you.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:50.340
My life is with you.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.340
For better or for worse?

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.340
For richer or for poorer.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:59.029
Lois, what are you talking about?

00:09:59.029 --> 00:10:00.029
You're absolutely right.

00:10:00.029 --> 00:10:03.029
What kind of adjective is poorer?

00:10:03.029 --> 00:10:08.039
Somebody is gonna need an editor.

00:10:08.039 --> 00:10:09.039
For their vows.

00:10:09.039 --> 00:10:12.639
Right.

00:10:12.639 --> 00:10:14.639
You know Lois, there's something at the office

00:10:14.639 --> 00:10:17.639
that I need to investigate.

00:10:17.639 --> 00:10:19.639
All right, Mr. Coldfeet.

00:10:19.639 --> 00:10:21.639
I'll keep the home fires burning.

00:10:21.639 --> 00:10:26.399
Rain check on talking about the big events for now.

00:10:26.399 --> 00:10:27.399
You better make an honest woman.

00:10:27.399 --> 00:10:50.649
out of me, Clark Kent.

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:51.649
Security!

00:10:51.649 --> 00:10:54.649
I'm afraid they're otherwise engaged.

00:10:54.649 --> 00:10:55.649
No. No.

00:10:55.649 --> 00:11:02.990
I like you just where you are.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:06.879
Then maybe you'd like to join me.

00:11:06.879 --> 00:11:12.529
You're already in bed with someone else.

00:11:12.529 --> 00:11:21.179
Wrong choice of bedfellows.

00:11:21.179 --> 00:11:26.620
I'm moments away from completing my tower.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.620
I thought you needed the book of Rao to finish it.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.620
We found another way.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:36.620
And it seems your satellite systems are lagging behind schedule.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:38.620
We're onlining the safety.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:39.620
tests now.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:41.620
I'll handle that, thank you.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:42.620
Only I can run them.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:46.690
Well, I've got your fingerprints,

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:49.690
so I can access all of the networking data without you.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:50.690
Cheers.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:58.289
You're digging your own grave.

00:11:58.289 --> 00:12:04.809
You better make sure there's room in there for both of us.

00:12:04.809 --> 00:12:11.100
You neglected to tell me

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.100
that Callow will supply new identities to my people.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:33.649
There are no more your people than they are his.

00:12:33.649 --> 00:12:38.649
And eventually, he will be their leader.

00:12:38.649 --> 00:12:43.679
And don't underestimate their leader.

00:12:43.679 --> 00:12:45.679
underestimate their loyalty to me.

00:12:45.679 --> 00:12:50.019
But they don't see you as the savior that he is.

00:12:50.019 --> 00:12:52.019
There's blood on your hands.

00:12:52.019 --> 00:12:55.019
You're tainted, a reminder of their past.

00:12:55.019 --> 00:12:57.019
He's the promise for their future.

00:12:57.019 --> 00:13:03.700
It's what you've always wanted, isn't it?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:06.700
Help give my people their powers so they can save your doom planet.

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:11.649
Over the reins to Calone, then what?

00:13:11.649 --> 00:13:16.059
Hmm? Get rid of me.

00:13:16.059 --> 00:13:21.850
If necessary, we need the knowledge of your people

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.850
to help us reverse the damage we've done here.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:27.850
done here to show mercy to this planet.

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:38.659
When I take over those satellites tomorrow,

00:13:38.659 --> 00:13:40.659
and when I gain my own powers,

00:13:40.659 --> 00:13:46.299
be the one who needs mercy.

00:13:46.299 --> 00:14:08.360
Louis!

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:12.360
Well, it is amazing what four hours of scrubbing a kitchen can do.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:15.360
It simply sparkles.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.360
Okay, let's open a window.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:21.360
I think you may have gotten a contact tie with that lemony, fresh scent.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.360
And why is your vinyl collection here?

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.360
Drum roll, please.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.559
Drum roll, please.

00:14:27.559 --> 00:14:33.250
Shea Kent has a new resident.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.090
I moved in.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:35.830
Great.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.590
We can have you move back to the Talon

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:39.830
and all packed up before the sun's up.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.990
I'm sorry that you're having a hard time with this, Chloe,

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.370
but this love train has left the station.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.309
No, the love train has jumped the tracks.

00:14:47.309 --> 00:14:48.470
I've seen Clark in love before,

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:49.769
and it always holds him back.

00:14:49.769 --> 00:14:50.470
You know what?

00:14:52.529 --> 00:14:54.029
It is just a little sad that the only way

00:14:54.029 --> 00:14:55.409
that you can get close to Clark right now

00:14:55.409 --> 00:14:56.629
is to play Mother Hen.

00:14:56.629 --> 00:14:58.570
Clark is a very private person.

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.509
And when the chips are down, everyone can see your cards.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:02.049
Hey!

00:15:04.049 --> 00:15:05.750
Clark knows that he can trust me.

00:15:06.149 --> 00:15:06.809
Just like the blur?

00:15:07.809 --> 00:15:09.830
When you were secretly talking to him

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:12.169
and you announced it to everyone on national television?

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:19.259
I never planned for it to happen that way.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:21.059
Okay, well, let's, look, you know what?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.340
As long as I've known you, you have always had to have the scoop.

00:15:23.419 --> 00:15:25.440
But when it comes to understanding the real, Clark,

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.419
you are always going to be a second string.

00:15:39.519 --> 00:15:42.419
You know, this whole Martha Stewart makeover thing

00:15:42.419 --> 00:15:43.519
isn't fooling anyone.

00:15:44.659 --> 00:15:47.159
Once Clark knows you, the real you,

00:15:47.159 --> 00:15:49.100
underneath all of this lowest armor,

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.340
he's gonna see that you're just a scared little kid

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:55.919
who runs away the second anything goes wrong.

00:15:55.919 --> 00:15:58.179
If you really love him,

00:15:58.179 --> 00:16:24.389
the best thing you can do for Clark is leave him.

00:16:24.389 --> 00:16:27.519
Excuse me.

00:16:27.519 --> 00:16:29.860
You sold my friend and I some candies the other night.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:33.200
Yeah, that's right.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.039
You're with a bitter chick.

00:16:36.039 --> 00:16:38.080
Right, well, the bitter chick isn't feeling so good.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.279
She kind of got sick.

00:16:39.279 --> 00:16:41.620
I'm retracing her steps.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.220
Was there anything

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:44.240
in that chocolate you sold there?

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.240
Uh, yeah, fat.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.240
I ate two boxes and gained three pounds.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:17:00.379
Thanks.

00:17:00.379 --> 00:17:02.379
Fairy dust, that was cute.

00:17:02.379 --> 00:17:04.380
Where'd you get it?

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:07.380
Yeah, I don't know what it is, but it comes from some Corey

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.380
in Smallville.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.380
Meteorog.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:22.309
Is that your girlfriend?

00:17:22.309 --> 00:17:24.309
Oh, she's not my...

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:28.140
We don't use that word.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:36.339
Lois?

00:17:36.339 --> 00:17:38.339
Are you all right? What's the emergency?

00:17:38.339 --> 00:17:54.359
Are you sure?

00:17:54.359 --> 00:17:56.359
Because you seem kind of...

00:17:56.359 --> 00:18:04.380
Kind of pathetic.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.380
Father going through the motions, Clark.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:09.380
This whole moving-in thing together was a joke.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.380
You're not yourself right now.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:13.380
Come on, I'm not stupid.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:17.380
I can tell that you just hated that burnt brick of meat.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:20.380
Let's get you some water.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:23.380
Just stop trying to sugarcoat it, Clark.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:27.619
For you, Clark.

00:18:27.619 --> 00:18:29.619
Chloe was right to protect you from me.

00:18:29.619 --> 00:18:32.619
Well, Chloe can be overprotective sometimes.

00:18:32.619 --> 00:18:39.200
No. She hit the target head on.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.200
She said that I was going to wreck us, and she's right.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:46.599
Clark, I don't...

00:18:46.599 --> 00:18:51.599
I don't know the first thing about family time or dinners at home.

00:18:51.599 --> 00:18:53.599
I don't...

00:18:53.599 --> 00:18:56.599
I'm glad that you're opening up to me.

00:18:56.599 --> 00:18:59.599
But there's something else going on here.

00:18:59.599 --> 00:19:04.160
You're right.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:12.950
Something is going on.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:13.950
I've made a fool of my son.

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:18.900
long enough. It hurts me to be around you.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:24.099
I have to leave you, Clark.

00:19:24.099 --> 00:19:29.660
Leave Smallville.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.660
Lois, you need to sleep on this.

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:37.289
I promise things will look better in the morning.

00:19:37.289 --> 00:19:39.289
No, they won't.

00:19:39.289 --> 00:19:41.289
Clark, I'm a big girl.

00:19:41.289 --> 00:19:43.289
I can pull myself up by my own bootstraps.

00:19:43.289 --> 00:19:44.289
Thank you very much.

00:19:44.289 --> 00:19:45.289
I just...

00:19:45.289 --> 00:19:47.289
I'd hope that somehow I'd be able to pull it off.

00:19:47.289 --> 00:19:49.289
The whole making a home thing.

00:19:49.289 --> 00:19:51.289
Oh, stop. You are home.

00:19:51.289 --> 00:20:02.630
Home is for real.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.630
For always.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:09.759
forever. Goodbye.

00:20:09.759 --> 00:20:10.759
Is Mova?

00:20:10.759 --> 00:20:12.759
Lois, you can't leave, not yet.

00:20:12.759 --> 00:20:19.019
I promise. We'll be together.

00:20:19.019 --> 00:20:21.019
Always and...

00:20:21.019 --> 00:20:32.369
Forever. Do you mean it?

00:20:32.369 --> 00:20:48.920
I do.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:21:05.420
I guess we can move my stuff out of the guest room now.

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:06.420
Clark, it's good you're here.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:09.420
